<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Mayne, Brambles firm after TNT bid.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Mayne, Brambles firm after TNT bid.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in transport firms Mayne Nickless Ltd and Brambles Industries Ltd firmed in active early Wednesday trade after Dutch telecoms and post company KPN bid for fellow transport company TNT Ltd.</p>
<p>The A$2.45 per share bid was 50 percent above TNT's closing price on Tuesday -- valuing it at A$2 billion -- had buoyed demand for transport stocks overall, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a re-rating going on,&quot; James Capel director of institutional sales Stephen Streeter said. Mayne Nickless' shares were up 14 cents at A$8.85 by 10.45 am (0045 GMT) while Brambles' shares were up 25 cents at A$20.75.  </p>
<p>TNT shares were untraded. They last traded on Tuesday at A$1.63, up two cents on the day.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
